# /etc/immich-integrity-exceptions
#
# Asset UUIDs whose file on disk disagrees with Immich's recorded checksum,
# investigated and found NOT to be disk corruption. One UUID per line.
# verify_immich_source_integrity.sh skips these but still reports the count.
#
# 2026-08-28 -- the three largest videos in the library. For each, WBU and
# FleetNAS hold IDENTICAL bytes (two independent reads agreeing) and the files
# are structurally valid; only Immich's database disagrees, and it disagrees
# with both copies rather than matching either.
#
# Immich streams the whole file through memory to hash it at ingest, so a
# multi-gigabyte video passes ~1000x more data through RAM than a photo does.
# All three were ingested between 2026-06-22 and 2026-08-22, inside the window
# when this machine ran four mismatched DIMMs. Every asset under ~150 MB
# matched its record; only the multi-GB ones did not. The recorded checksums
# are the corrupted values, not the files.
#
# Re-check these if Immich ever recomputes checksums; the entries can be
# removed once the database agrees with the disk again.

45d01a4e-a5b6-46c6-84a4-2c779be21f26   # 5.4 GB mp4
9d8cb158-b14f-4477-bca2-d204ffa90773   # 2.0 GB mp4
c81cb913-6860-4bbf-b9fc-adb7727703d2   # 3.0 GB mp4
